29:`WatchSession` publishes one immutable `Revision` at a time: global source data, the named-type index, resolved components with their recorded dependencies, diagnostics and the assembled output. An update builds the next revision off to the side and publishes it with one atomic store, so a reader sees one complete revision. Cold extraction and watch revisions share `Revision::assemble()`, and a watch snapshot equals a cold extract of the same files (see `docs/architecture/pipeline-orchestration.md`).
31:Between parse and resolve, the declarations of installed packages that project types name are loaded by name into a shared `DependencyLayer` (`dependency_types.rs`, on by default; ADR 0010). A lazy session (`WatchSession::lazy`, ADR 0016) parses and indexes every file but resolves a component only when a request names it, which is how the Storybook addon runs; every answer equals the batch extraction's for the same key. A session can also ask a warm TypeScript 7.1 checker for the requested component (`semanticTypes: 'on-demand'`, ADR 0022), experimental and off by default.
60:`crates/core` has no dependency on async runtimes, NAPI, or terminal libraries. It can be linked from any host. `crates/semantic` and `crates/tsc-client` are published crates, always compiled into the CLI and the binding and enabled at run time (ADR 0007); Callisto publishes them before the CLI.
100:  deps.rs         — what a component's resolution depended on, for watch-mode re-resolution
117:dependency_types.rs — dependency declarations loaded by name before resolution into a shared layer (ADR 0010)
183:The merged view across all parsed files: component declarations, type aliases, interface definitions, import bindings. Today `WatchSession` publishes this map independently via `ArcSwap`. Under the target watch invariant above it becomes one member of the immutable aggregate `WatchRevision`, so readers load one coherent published revision.
189:`react-docgen-typescript` creates a TypeScript `Program` — this loads all imported types transitively, runs type inference, and is single-threaded. `caliper-docgen` parses each file independently in parallel with no type-checking pass. The trade-off: TypeScript-only semantics (conditional types, `infer`, deep utility type evaluation) fall through to `{ kind: "opaque" }`. Everything structurally expressible — interfaces, intersections, unions, `Omit`, `Pick`, `VariantProps` — resolves correctly.
205:`.d.ts` files from `node_modules` rarely change within a project session. The cache stores parsed `SourceData` keyed by file path and content hash, serialized with msgpack and written atomically, and is discarded whenever the build that wrote it differs (the payload's header carries the schema version, the crate version and a source fingerprint). `node_modules/.cache/` is the correct location: it is cleaned with `node_modules`, excluded from version control, and preserved across CI runs when `node_modules` is cached by layer.
223:Config file loading is fully implemented. Imports resolve across packages when the imported file is under a source directory, and the declarations of installed packages that project types name are loaded by default (`--no-load-dependencies` turns that off). See `docs/STATUS.md` if you're checking whether an older doc's claim about either is still true.

